  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1113 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nHot conditions will continue underneath a 600 dam ridge with\nafternoon highs reaching the upper 90s to low 100s. Starting\nThursday, the ridge will begin to slowly retrograde west as a\ntropical wave approaches Florida. Despite the westerly movement,\nnear record to record highs are forecast through the weekend. The\nHeat Advisory has been extended through 8 PM Saturday for the\nentire forecast area. Given the prolonged nature of this heat,\nvulnerable populations are at the greatest risk for developing\nheat-related illness. Remember to regularly check on neighbors\nand ensure ample hydration over the coming days.\n\nBoth the GFS and ECMWF depict a shortwave developing to the lee\nof the Rockies on Sunday. This feature will send a weak frontal\nboundary into the Mid-South late Monday into Tuesday. Rain\nchances will increase, but we are still not anticipating a\nwidespread rainfall event. Temperatures will decrease a few\ndegrees by the middle of next week, but above-average highs are\nfavored through the end of the month.\n\nANS",
